Spec: Boundary Tests

Platform: Python/unittest

Purpose:
  Guard the provider-neutral core boundaries, canonical agent procedure, concrete agent materialization, Spec Kit change-system projection, native authorization and verification, migration compatibility evidence, installation wiring, packaging path, and deterministic output with focused tests that avoid duplicating production logic.

Owns:
  ./test_boundary_core_layout.py
  ./test_native_contract_parsing.py
  ./test_native_contract_graph.py
  ./test_native_contract_context.py
  ./test_native_contract_cli.py
  ./test_authorization_model.py
  ./test_authorization_lifecycle.py
  ./test_operation_record.py
  ./test_native_verification.py
  ./test_spec_kit_adapter.py
  ./test_agent_skills.py
  ./test_agent_skill_materialization.py
  ./test_boundary.py
  ./boundary_test_support.py
  ./boundary_test_paths.py
  ./boundary_test_resolver.py
  ./boundary_test_ownership.py
  ./boundary_test_output.py
  ./boundary_test_fixture.py
  ./test_change_boundary_schema.py
  ./test_validation.py
  ./validation_test_tasks.py
  ./validation_test_engine.py
  ./validation_test_support.py
  ./validation_test_fixture.py
  ./test_verification.py
  ./verification_test_git.py
  ./verification_test_engine.py
  ./verification_test_fixture.py
  ./test_preset.py
  ./preset_test_support.py
  ./preset_test_install_support.py
  ./preset_test_source.py
  ./preset_test_install.py
  ./preset_test_distribution.py
  ./test_workflow.py
  ./workflow_test_source.py
  ./workflow_test_gate.py

References:
  /integration/specdd/scripts/scripts.sdd
  /integration/specdd/schemas/change-boundary.schema.json
  /integration/specdd/workflow-overlay.sdd
  /integration/specdd-preset/specdd-preset.sdd
  /scripts/scripts.sdd
  ./fixtures/specdd-two-domain/specdd-two-domain.sdd

Must:
  Native core layout tests keep repository/path, contract, target-context, authorization, verification, and CLI boundaries importable from ./src/boundary without provider-specific implementation names.
  Native contract parsing tests cover deterministic discovery under contracts/, boundary.contract/v1 frontmatter, exact and subtree scope grammar, recognized semantic-section extraction, source provenance, and deterministic content identities.
  Native contract graph/context tests cover deterministic indexes, exact and nested ownership, additive applicability, ambiguity rejection, missing intended targets, direct dependency interfaces, semantic provenance, and deterministic projection.
  Native CLI tests cover contract-check diagnostics, multi-target inspection of absent intended targets, stable provenance-rich output, and absence of persisted projections.
  Native authorization-model tests cover canonical explicit task writes, task identity/order preservation, duplicate rejection, and ordered change-level write projection.
  Native authorization-lifecycle tests cover implementation-before-authorization rejection, verified epoch replacement, scope expansion, exact predecessor carry-forward, concurrent dirty mutation, deletion, staging/index transitions, immutable predecessor archival, and Git HEAD changes.
  Native operation-record tests cover atomic evidence content and storage, including failed successor replacement after verified predecessor closure.
  Native verification tests derive actual writes from Git, reject undeclared writes even within an already represented owner, reject native-contract writes during implementation, fresh-resolve changed target context, keep contract-evolution write-kind checks separate from structural validation, and allow adapter-owned generated state to be excluded without hiding authorized targets.
  Spec Kit adapter tests project task identity and exact writes only from dedicated structured `Writes:` metadata and ignore incidental path-looking prose.
  Spec Kit adapter lifecycle tests authorize native Boundary operations from fresh task projection and exclude deterministic host-owned feature state during Git-derived verification.
  Public Spec Kit integration exposes only Boundary authorization and verification wrappers; planning context and task validation are not public lifecycle states.
  The Spec Kit workflow overlay owns implementation-entry authorization and implementation-exit verification without duplicated extension hooks.
  The small task preset adds exact write metadata and on-demand inspection guidance without augmenting planning or convergence commands.
  Canonical agent-skill tests keep scope, implementation, and contract-evolution procedure small, vendor-neutral, free of volatile operation values, and explicit about deterministic lifecycle boundaries.
  Agent materialization tests cover deterministic Codex discovery paths, runtime frontmatter separated from canonical procedure, exact canonical bodies, stable bytes across unrelated feature operations, and a second concrete Claude Code materialization without generalized runtime-adapter machinery.
  Schema tests reuse the legacy migration bridge schema validator instead of maintaining an independent JSON Schema implementation.
  Legacy adapter tests preserve path normalization, resolver-backed ownership derivation, deterministic output, and schema validation coverage until P9 removes SpecDD migration compatibility.
  Existing-target and intended-target compatibility remain migration evidence rather than native Boundary semantics.
  Effective-context migration tests prove ownership-preserving legacy governing-context changes alter their deterministic compatibility identity.
  Legacy authorization tests prove changed effective SpecDD context blocks legacy snapshot creation while failed reauthorization preserves prior compatibility evidence.
  Tests distinguish missing external executables from resolver, lint, and ownership diagnostics.
  The real two-domain fixture remains temporary migration evidence while the repository is converted to native contracts.
  Successful native authorization stores its operation record outside the worktree in Git metadata.
  Git verification separates implementation writes from change-system state through adapter classification without allowing that classification to hide native contracts or authorized targets.
  Changed persistent contracts do not retroactively authorize implementation in the same operation.
  Preset installation tests exercise registrar-backed adapter command materialization, task composition, workflow-overlay installation, Boundary skill materialization, and clean removal.
  Distribution installation tests exercise local installation, Codex switching, generated native Boundary runtime state, stable Boundary skill bytes, clean remove/reinstall, and an immutable GitHub archive path without depending on live network access.
  Distribution installation tests prove an isolated downstream consumer with native contracts and no canonical Boundary implementation source can authorize and verify through installed adapter runtime.
  Distribution installation tests reject mutable GitHub branch archives.
  Static source tests cover only packaging and lifecycle wiring that is not already established more directly by behavioral or installation tests.
  Workflow gate tests preserve legacy migration helper determinism while workflow source tests prove only native authorization and verification are structurally integrated.
